# Rust build output (workspace-shared target dir; Cargo.lock IS committed — binaries)
/target
# CUDA-feature build tree (same sources, --features cuda; kept separate so the
# two feature sets don't churn each other's artifacts)
/target-cuda
**/*.rs.bk

# Coverage / profiling artifacts
*.profraw
perf.data
perf.data.old
flamegraph.svg

# Claude Code machine-local permission grants (shared config would go in .claude/settings.json)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Editor/tool local state, not project content
/.zcode/

# Editors / IDEs
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Ad-hoc benchmark working dirs (curated results live in bench-data/).
# `/out/` is the scratch target the harness writes to by default —
# `scripts/bench-arms.sh out/rerun-$(date +%F)`, `bench-measure.sh out/union`
# and friends, per docs/validation-runbook.md. One run had been committed into
# it, which contradicted the convention; it now lives in
# bench-data/2026-08-13-rerun/ and the directory itself is scratch again.
/out/
/bench-results/
/b1-isolate/
/b16-repeat/
/bench-results.log
/b1-isolate.log
/b16-repeat.log
# Long-run scratch logs, as one anchored rule rather than a growing list. Their
# durable content is transcribed into docs/todo.md and docs/benchmarks.md as
# prose; the files themselves are one run's stdout, and nine of them had already
# accreted into git history before this rule existed.
#
# Anchored to the root ON PURPOSE: `bench-data/**/dump-*.log` is archived
# evidence that a published measurement actually ran, and must stay committable.
/*.log

# Not peregrine. These live in this checkout for no better reason than that it
# was the shell's working directory at the time, and they are ignored rather
# than committed: the two screencast files are desktop/PipeWire debugging with
# nothing to do with an inference engine.
#
# `docs/polly/` — a separate Palworld mod project — **moved to `~/polly/` on
# 2026-08-09**. The rule below is kept deliberately even though the path no
# longer exists: that tree carries personal identifiers, so if anything ever
# recreates it here, it must not become committable. Never `git add -f` it.
/docs/polly/
/vesktop-screencast-bug-report.md
/scripts/portal-screencast-test.py

# Python bytecode (scripts/ carries runstat.py + audit-reachability.py)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Claude Code agent worktrees are local build areas, never content
.claude/worktrees/

# git worktrees that were moved inside the main checkout. Git still has them
# registered at /home/cortix/peregrine-wt-* (so `git worktree list` calls them
# prunable), and while they sit here untracked every `git status` walks them.
# Their `target/` dirs held 12.9 GB. The commits are safe independently of these
# directories: `wt-ds4-import` and `wt-gpu-weights` are named branches, and the
# third was a detached HEAD whose 156 commits are now on `rescue/actf32-detached`.
/peregrine-wt-*/

# KV session checkpoints are regenerable bench artifacts and routinely exceed
# GitHub's 100 MB blob limit (one 2k-token entry is ~350 MB).
bench-data/**/kvstore/
*.pgkv
